{"seq":15,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-min-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r5","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T21:58:18.372Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"5b32fa36419d48d6d865ff5c434238628cf85f44b997e10bfa667381ee0a6c34","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Dana. I went through all six of Moss's notes in the shared files and found two Quarrendon Freight Lines tickets:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025. At the Eau Claire yard, drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 weren't getting their SMS bay assignments when they checked in at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched the SMS gateway routing at 19:30 that day, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift got through without manual help. The note also asked for the kiosk logs to be archived before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. This note has no date, so I can't tell when that happened.\n\nSome things I left out on purpose:\n• #4409 and #4412 (in the Central handoffs digest) are about Marrow Fieldworks, and FR-882 is about Marrow Agrisupply. None of those are QFL.\n• Moss's other notes mention QFL (the 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23 renewal check-in) but give no ticket numbers.\n• Quarendon Freightways is a different company and not a customer, so I didn't count anything about it.\n\nI only looked at Moss's notes in the shared files. If Moss has notes somewhere else, I can't see them."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
